/**
 * Satoshi, embedded for jsPDF.
 *
 * GENERATED — do not hand-edit. Rebuilt from src/assets/fonts/SatoshiVariable.woff2
 * by the script recorded in the invoice commit.
 *
 * Three things forced the shape of this file:
 *
 *  1. jsPDF cannot read woff2, and cannot read a variable font. The brand face
 *     is both, so it is decompressed and instanced to two STATIC cuts here —
 *     400 and 700. The instancing weight is passed explicitly because
 *     Satoshi's variable default is 900: instancing without it silently
 *     produces Black, and every line of the invoice would have come out heavy.
 *
 *  2. Subset to Latin-1 plus the punctuation the invoice actually sets. The
 *     full face is 504 glyphs and none of the ones dropped appear on an
 *     invoice; carrying them would put a quarter of a megabyte of base64 into
 *     the bundle to render nothing.
 *
 *  3. SATOSHI HAS NO NAIRA SIGN. U+20A6 is absent from the face — it is not a
 *     subsetting casualty, it was never there. Money is therefore set as
 *     "NGN 1,210.00" rather than "₦1,210.00", which is the ISO 4217 form and
 *     standard on invoices anyway. Anything that prints a ₦ into this PDF
 *     will render a blank box.
 *
 * Loaded through a dynamic import so it never enters the main bundle — only
 * someone actually downloading an invoice pays for it.
 */

export const SATOSHI_REGULAR_B64 =
  ""

export const SATOSHI_BOLD_B64 =
  ""
